KG42.register("clusters-62738bf9b777d477be0838c3",{"id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v142-d-CL003","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","label":"Net energy trading and basic revenues and expenditures at given internal prices","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL003","label":"Net energy trading and basic revenues and expenditures at given internal prices","market_meaning":"Given generation, consumption, and internal prices for the same period, prosumers buy from or sell to MGO according to the sign of net energy, generating corresponding seller-revenue or buyer-expenditure terms.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","activation","settlement"],"scope_disposition":"compatible","scope_explanation":"The three chains describe the product, execution direction, and base monetary terms of the same M01 period transaction. Both the positive-net-energy and non-positive-net-energy branches are retained; zero net energy produces zero trading quantity and a zero base monetary term. The condition excluding zero net energy in the response expression is not introduced, and M02 deviation charges are not included.","assembly_status":"assembled","boundary_rationale":"The net energy product, transaction counterparty and direction, price applicability, and basic revenues and expenditures jointly constitute an independently intelligible trading rule. Internal prices serve here as given inputs, while the optimization that generates them is handled by CL001.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R009","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Defines the net energy product for each prosumer as a trading input, retaining both verbal and mathematical definitions."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Specifies the direction of buying from or selling to MGO and the applicable internal prices under the two net-energy branches."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R010","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Maps the same transaction branches to base monetary terms expressed as seller revenue and buyer negative revenue."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL003-L001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-n","v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-Eg-n","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x-x_n","v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta-E_n^g","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e012"],"rationale":"Generation and consumption for the same period in the product definition enter the determination of the transaction branch, and the sign of net energy determines the transaction direction; the product definition and transaction obligations retain distinct uses."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL003-L002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e012","v141-b-g01-e014"],"rationale":"The selling and buying execution branches correspond respectively to revenue and negative revenue at the same prices and net energy. Transaction obligations and monetary terms are complementary and are not treated as duplicate constraints because their conditions are similar."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL003-M001","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::V::execution.energy_trade","v141-c-R010::V::execution.energy_trade"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R005::V::execution.energy_trade","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e012"],"rationale":"Both refer to internal net energy trading between this M01 prosumer and MGO; only the display entry point is unified."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL003-M002","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-n","v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x-x_n","v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-x-n"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e012","v141-b-g01-e015"],"rationale":"The same prosumer's consumption for a period is used respectively for product, execution, and revenue and expenditure calculations; each chain's existing domain descriptions are retained, and the bounds of one chain are not rewritten into other chains."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL003-M003","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-Eg-n","v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta-E_n^g","v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-Eng"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e012"],"rationale":"All represent the prosumer's PV generation in the same M01 trading period; the local input objects in the product, execution, and revenue and expenditure representations are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL003-M004","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta-p_s","v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-ps"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e014"],"rationale":"The price at which MGO purchases the seller's energy in the execution chain and the price used for seller revenue in the revenue and expenditure chain correspond to the same internal selling price."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL003-M005","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta-p_b","v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-pb"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e014"],"rationale":"The price at which MGO sells energy in the execution chain and the price used for buyer expenditure in the revenue and expenditure chain correspond to the same internal buying price; their local input roles remain unchanged."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL003-M006","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e012","v141-b-g01-e015"],"rationale":"The verbal and mathematical representations of the same net energy product definition are retained side by side; they are not counted as two independent product rules, and the original differences in bindings are not deleted."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G001","category":"unverified_source","description":"This cluster assembles only basic transaction revenues and expenditures, and the source evidence remains UNREVIEWED/unverified. The buyer term retains the negative-revenue sign used in utility and is not silently converted into an M02 bill object.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R009","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e012","v141-b-g01-e014","v141-b-g01-e015"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check buying and selling directions, price perspectives, and the signs of monetary terms; assembled does not indicate that the sources or downstream scientific interpretations have independently passed review."}]},"rule_refs":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R009","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R010"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-5d6a447386335cd5","COMP-c6917f781ea3f39e","KG31-36e0a27c810a788e","KG31-c38847500f58498d"]});
